  "html_url": "https://github.com/niway-dev/kaipu-record/pull/416#discussion_r4403370615",
  "body": "🟡🐛 **Consider · bug: Pause before first-media resolves is not tracked in videoClock**\n\n`videoClock` is only created when `firstMediaTimestamp` resolves. `pauseRecording` and `resumeRecording` skip it while it is null (lines 831, 841). If the user pauses and resumes before t0 resolves, that pause is never removed from the video duration. The spec lists this as the known pre-t0 pause gap and keeps it out of scope. It is not tested, though, so a test that pins the accepted behaviour would help."
 },
